    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** Microsoft Mage-Flow (4B) text to image from the Comfy-Org int8 file, 20 steps, 1024x1024 by default. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Prompt**: describe the picture, in English.\n   - **Negative prompt**: what to avoid. Empty in the template.\n   - **Size**: pick the shape; megapixels 1 = 1024x1024 (16:9 = 1360x768). The model card gives 512 to 2048 px per side (only 1024x1024 and 1360x768 were run here). Leave \"multiple\" at 16.\n   - **Steps** (20) and **CFG** (5): 20 is the authors' step count for this RL-aligned file (the template has 30: nearly the same picture, 1.5x the time); CFG 5 is the template's.\n   - **Seed**: fixed at 24112026, so the first Run gives the README picture. Type a new number (or set \"control after generate\" to randomize) for a new picture; Run with nothing changed does nothing.\n2. **Models**: the three loaders must show the files from the Downloads note. Nothing to change.\n3. **Prompt**: nothing to change; text and size come from group 1. More pictures per run: `batch_size` on this node.\n4. **Sampling**: euler / simple, from the template.\n5. Press **Run**. The picture is saved by the **Result** node to `output/Mage-Flow/` as PNG.\n\n**What to expect:** one 1024x1024 or 1360x768 picture in 8 to 9 s once the models are loaded, 11 s for the first run of a fresh ComfyUI (RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB). The template's 30 steps took 12 s.\n\n**Text in the picture:** put the words in quotes. The sample sign came out right in 3 of 3 seeds.\n\n**Tested on:** RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, ComfyUI 0.45.3, 2026-11-24. Not verified on a 12 GB card.\n"
   ]
  },
